adjudication.rationale:
In packages/core/EventManager.ts the diff replaces optional chaining with array destructuring:

```ts
const [mainHostDestinationCalendar] = evt.destinationCalendar ?? [];
if (evt.location === MeetLocationType && mainHostDestinationCalendar.integration !== "google_calendar") {
  evt["location"] = "integrations:daily";
}
```

If `evt.destinationCalendar` is `null` or `[]`, destructuring yields `undefined`, and `mainHostDestinationCalendar.integration` will throw a TypeError. The diff also shows multiple call sites now explicitly setting `destinationCalendar` to `[]` (e.g. bookingReminder.ts, webhook handlers), making this reachable. The previous code (`evt.destinationCalendar?.integration`) would not throw and would still trigger the fallback.
